# AI and Nutrition Rules

- Read `/docs/AI_NUTRITION_SAFETY.md`.
- Treat image recognition as probabilistic.
- Return candidate foods rather than claiming certainty.
- Allow user confirmation and correction.
- Support manual food search when recognition fails.
- Show serving basis and nutrition source.
- Preserve unknown nutrient values.
- Never fabricate nutrition values.
- Never label AI output as institution-verified.
- Clearly distinguish mock recognition from external AI recognition.
- Do not infer exact ingredients, allergens, oil quantity, recipe proportions, or serving weight from an image.
- Do not provide diagnosis or treatment recommendations.
